QuakeAVP — authors

The port
--------

A. Cervantez — the visionOS port in its entirety: the SwiftUI app shell and
engine host, the Metal renderer (Sources/QuakeRenderer, including the shaders
and the engine-side bridge), the platform layer that replaces SDL and OpenGL
(Sources/QuakeCore/platform), the capture and export pipeline, and the tools
under tools/.

Every file listed above carries an SPDX identifier and a copyright line.

The engine
----------

QuakeAVP carries QuakeSpasm 0.97 under Sources/QuakeCore/engine, vendored
unmodified apart from six marked hunks. Its authorship is id Software's and
the QuakeSpasm team's, recorded in the per-file notices in that directory and
in the engine's own history; UPSTREAM.md records the exact commit, what was
taken, what was left behind and every patch applied.

Third-party single-file libraries are credited in UPSTREAM.md with their
sources and pinned revisions: stb_vorbis (Sean Barrett), lodepng (Lode
Vandevenne) and miniz (Rich Geldreich, RAD Game Tools, Valve).

Quake and the Quake logo are trademarks of id Software LLC. QuakeAVP is an
unofficial port and ships no game data.
